# FOAM git & delivery safety

## Never automatic

Without an **explicit request in the current conversation**, do **not**:

- `git commit`
- `git push` (any form)
- force push
- `firebase deploy` (any target)
- deploy Hosting, Functions, Firestore rules, or indexes
- change production infrastructure as a side effect of coding
- treat deployment as an invisible final step

User-rule git safety still applies: commit/push only when asked; no destructive git.

## Web “done”

Firebase Hosting deploy happens **only** when the user explicitly asks.

Do **not** define completion as “pushed + hosted” unless they requested that.

## Mobile “done”

Mobile work must **not** define done as a Firebase Hosting deployment.

Completion means:

- code implemented
- tests pass (when present)
- local/dev build works
- emulator/device verification completed
- EAS Build **only** when explicitly requested

App Store / Google Play submission is **never** automatic.

Prefer Expo Development Builds for day-to-day mobile work.
